Third-party references and their licenses
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

eos/messages.py, eos/params.py
  The SysEx frame layout, command set, and parameter ID tables are transcribed
  from the manufacturer's own protocol specification:
    "Remote Preset Editing via MIDI SysEx", Draft #30, EOS 4.00
    Brian Clark, E-mu Systems, 17 February 1999
  That document is NOT redistributed with this project.

  Most of what is taken from it is wire-protocol fact used as data — command
  bytes, parameter ids, value ranges, and the specification's own names for
  parameters and enumerated values.

  One exception, stated plainly: the specification also contains a small
  amount of C source for the display conversions that turn a raw parameter
  value into the number the front panel shows, and the following functions in
  eos/params.py follow it directly rather than being independently derived:

    fil_freq()          a port of the spec's fil_freq(input, maxfreq, mul)
    filter_table_1/2/3  its (maxfreq, mul) arguments per Filter Tables 1-3
    cnv_morph_freq()    per the spec's Filter Table 5

  These are a few lines of arithmetic each, reproduced for interoperability —
  to display the same value the device itself displays — and E-mu / Creative
  Technology Ltd. retain whatever rights subsist in the original. If that
  is unacceptable to the rights holder, these functions can be removed or
  reimplemented from observed input/output behaviour without affecting any
  other part of this project.

  Everything else here is original work. Released under GPL-2.0-or-later.

eos/bridge.py
  The throttled-output queue (ThrottledOut), the MultiIn merged-input facade,
  the ALSA-client leak fix, and the MIDI port-enumeration helpers are ported
  from the sibling k2kremote project (k2kremote/midi_bridge.py), which itself
  ports them from:
    mpc2emu (tests/re_banks/krz_sysex_live.py)
    Copyright (C) 2025-2026  mpc2emu contributors
    License: GNU General Public License v2.0 or later (GPL-2.0-or-later)
  Both k2kremote and mpc2emu are sibling projects by the same author, also
  released under GPL-2.0-or-later. The rest of this file (EosBridge, the
  config.toml read/write helpers) is original work.

eos/params.py (LFO rate display)
  cnv_lfo_rate()'s byte->Hz coefficients are NOT from the E-mu specification --
  its LFO rate display table could not be transcribed unambiguously (the source
  wraps across a PDF page boundary). They are the sibling mpc2emu project's
  empirical calibration, measured from the E4XT's own rate menu:
    mpc2emu models/common.py, lfo_rate_byte_to_hz()
    Copyright (C) 2025-2026  mpc2emu contributors
    License: GNU General Public License v2.0 or later (GPL-2.0-or-later)

eosed/app.py
  Mostly original work, except: the key-hint legend's fold-to-terminal-width
  algorithm (wrap_blocks) is ported from the sibling k2kremote project
  (k2kremote/app.py's wrap_blocks), same author, released under
  GPL-2.0-or-later.

All other files (eos/__init__.py, eosed/__init__.py, eosed/cli.py,
eosed/demo.py, tests/, tools/)
  Original work. Released under GPL-2.0-or-later.

